{ "answer": ["POTS","Postural Orthostatic Tachycardia Syndrome","POTS syndrome"], "clues": ["This condition was first described by physician Jacob Mendes Da Costa in 1871 during the American Civil War. It frequently affected young soldiers and was sometimes known as De Costa syndrome around that time","The modern name of this syndrome came in 1982 and was formally defined by the Mayo Clinic in 1993. It can sometimes be triggered by viral or immune-system events and data shows that diagnoses of this disease increased 2-5 fold post-COVID 19 pandemic. This helped it gain a distinct ICD-10 code in 2022.","This is a disorder of the autonomic nervous system where people experience a sustained heart rate increase upon standing."] },
