{ "answer": ["Metolazone","zaroxolyn"], "clues": ["In a 2020 study, scientists screened an extensive library of existing, off-patent drugs to see if any could combat aging. They discovered that this drug significantly extends the lifespan of wild-type C. elegans otherwise known as the roundworm through activating the mitochondrial repair pathway.","Though this drug behaves similarly to thiazide diuretics, it is technically classified as a quinazoline-sulfonamide. Unlike true thiazides that lose effectiveness as the patient's kidney function drops, this drug maintains its potency even in advanced chronic kidney disease.","In the mid-20th century, the discovery of powerful loop diuretics revolutionized the treatment of severe fluid retention. However, doctors quickly ran into a major obstacle where a patient’s kidneys adapt to loop diuretics and stop responding. The introduction of this drug provided a major clinical breakthrough, as its unique chemical structure allowed it to be paired sequentially with loop diuretics to break through this resistance and safely restart fluid removal"] },
