{ "answer": ["Ticagrelor","brilinta"], "clues": ["Scientists used the chemical blueprint of ATP as their starting point for developing this drug, creating a new chemical class called cyclopentyl-triazolo-pyrimidines (CPTPs)","Despite showing superior reduction in cardiovascular deaths compared to clopidogrel globally in its landmark PLATO trial (2009), the data showed this drug was highly effective everywhere in the world except North America. They found that North American doctors routinely prescribed a higher daily maintenance dose of aspirin which chemically interfered with this drug's efficacy. This led to a permanent boxed warning stating it should only be taking with a low-dose baby aspirin","Before this drug, all standard oral P2Y12 inhibitors were irreversible. This was the first approved reversible oral antiplatelet agent and is currently preferred over clopidogrel for most patients with acute coronary syndrome"] },



